# NOTE: this file is written and must be read via nitransforms
# (nitransforms.linear.load(path, fmt='fs').matrix), not FreeSurfer's own LTA
# tools -- nitransforms stores LTAs using FreeSurfer's "points convention",
# so the raw matrix numbers above are NOT the intended physical transform
# directly; only round-tripping through nitransforms' reader/writer gives
# back the correct matrix.
# Maps HiP-CT brain native physical space (mm, corner-origin: voxel (0,0,0) -> RAS
# (0,0,0), any pyramid level) to true MNI RAS.
# UPDATED 2026-09-04: extracted the same way as the previous (2026-08-31)
# version -- Matrix = dst.affine @ inv(src.affine), src = the raw native
# sample volume's own identity/corner-origin header -- but with dst now
# pointing at the just-completed inverted-contrast nitorch registration run
# (finest pyramid level, "=== all levels complete ===").
# This works because nitorch's "Minimal reslice" never resamples the voxel
# array -- it only updates the NIfTI header's affine to bake in each new
# correction on top of the previous one -- so this level_0 moved file's own
# shape is still exactly (293,293,337), identical to raw native's, and its
# header already has the *entire* chain (prealign -> first-pass correction ->
# this run's two-level affine refinement) composed into it.
